{
    "test_name": "MOB.122_Map_Create_Work",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.122_Map_Create_Work",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.122` Create a work order from the **Mobile Map** \u2014 the last uncovered create entry\npoint.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **LEAVES RESIDUE**: a real work order per run, tagged `DD SYNTHETIC MOBILE`.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **The only mobile test with a third-party dependency.** Suggestions come from\n  Mapbox's geocoding API, so an outage or rate limit fails this for reasons unrelated to\n  MentorTwo. If it flaps, that is why \u2014 do not chase it as an app bug.\n- The popup is **not a button on the map**: it only exists once a geocoder result is\n  chosen. Type \u2192 pick a suggestion \u2192 the map flies there \u2192 `Add Work`. Every link in\n  that chain is asserted, so a failure names which one broke.\n- The query is \u22655 characters on purpose \u2014 the geocoder's `minLength: 5` means a shorter\n  term never queries at all and would look like a broken control. `limit: 2`, so\n  picking the first suggestion is safe.\n- No `defaultAsset` here, so the workflow list is not asset-filtered and `Datadog Test`\n  is findable by typing (unlike MOB.397 \u2014 see T2.1's note).",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Map",
            "Work Order",
            "CRUD",
            "residue"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
        "config": {
            "assertions": [],
            "config_variables": [
                {
                    "id": "fe7958bf-435f-4932-af8e-0931caab79e7",
                    "name": "MOBDEV",
                    "type": "global"
                },
                {
                    "name": "RUNID",
                    "type": "text",
                    "pattern": "{{ numeric(8) }}",
                    "example": "48120735"
                }
            ],
            "request": {
                "headers": {},
                "method": "GET",
                "url": "{{ MOBDEV }}"
            },
            "variables": [
